                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>
International Division was established as International Cell in 1996 with the mandate to promote bilateral and multilateral collaborations and to network with international educational institutions and inter-governmental agencies to provide opportunities for higher education to a larger segment internationally and to coordinate the international delegation and visits to the University.  The International Division in its objective of expanding the frontiers of IGNOU follows a four-fold approach of “Collaboration, cooperation, coordination and competition”.  International Division is the mini unit of all operation divisions and offers complete student support services to the overseas and foreign students residing in India like Admission, Examination, evaluation, award of degree and an integrated ICT support.  The University has also entrusted International Division as nodal centre for promoting, offering and monitoring online programmes for international students.
<li><b>Role and functions</b>
	<ul>
<li>Single window for International Operations of University.</li>
	<li>Recognition of Overseas Study Centres (OSCs).</li>
	<li>Complete student support services to the overseas and foreign students residing in India (FSRI).</li>
	<li>Coordinates the international delegation and visits to the University.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Objectives"  ><p><ul style="list-style-type:disc;">
					    <li>Expansion of IGNOU reach at international level through a four-fold approach of “Collaboration, cooperation, coordination and competition”.</li>
						<li>Internationalization of higher education through bilateral and multi-lateral collaborations. </li>
						<li>To network with international educational institutes of repute and inter-governmental agencies to provide opportunities for higher education to a larger segment internationally.</li>
						<li>Offering IGNOU’s academic programmes (ODL and online mode) in international arena. </li>
						<li>Promotion of Indian Knowledge System (IKS) internationally. </li>
						<li>To develop cultural, educational and scientific ties of cooperation, to encourage academic exchange and collaboration, and to advance education and training in the respective institutions through collaborations with educational institutes outside India.</li>
                     </ul>
</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="History"  ><p><ul>
	<li>International Division was established as International Cell in 1996 with the mandate to promote bilateral and multilateral collaborations and to network with international educational institutions and inter-governmental agencies to provide opportunities for higher education to a larger segment internationally and to coordinate the international delegation and visits to the University. </li>
	<li>The International Division in its objective of expanding the frontiers of IGNOU follows a four-fold approach of “Collaboration, cooperation, coordination and competition”. </li>
	<li>International Division is the mini unit of all operation divisions and offers complete student support services to the overseas and foreign students residing in India like Admission, Examination, evaluation, award of degree and an integrated ICT support. </li>
	<li>The University has also entrusted International Division as nodal centre for promoting, offering and monitoring online programmes for international students.  </li>
	</ul>
</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Achievements"  ><p>Keeping the objective of National Education Policy 2020 i.e. internationalization of higher education in focus, the University has taken many initiatives. At present, the University has its presence in 88 countries through various agreements/projects including 25 Overseas Study Centres (OSCs) spread over 15 foreign countries. The cumulative enrolment of international students is around 92000.</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-5" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>
International Division is committed to provide opportunities for higher education to a larger segment internationally through various international collaborations of mutual benefits. For expansion of the international presence of the University, we are following a four-fold approach of “Collaboration, cooperation, coordination and competition”.</p>
<p>At present, we offer 168 programmes through Open & Distance Learning (ODL) Mode through Universities/Institutions identified as its Overseas Study Centres internationally.  The very objective of this initiative is to impart quality higher education through open and distance learning mode on mutual benefit basis.  The programmes are offered in various disciplines at certificate, diploma, pg diploma, undergraduate and postgraduate level.  We register overseas students through 25 Overseas Study Centre located in 15 Countries.</p>
<p>Moreover, Foreign Students Residing in India (FSRI) may register in all academic programmes on offer for national students through any of our Regional Centres in India subject to fulfilment of educational and other requirements.</p>
<p>We offer complete student support services to the overseas and FSRI like Admission, Examination, evaluation, award of degree and an integrated ICT support.</p>
<p>International Division is also nodal centre for promoting, offering and monitoring online programmes for international students and a dedicated Learning Management System (LMS) portal has been provided for 44 online programmes on offer at present.</p>
<p>Further, for promoting online programmes of the University internationally, the University come out with a scheme of “Overseas Facilitator” and agreements have been signed with most of our existing OSCs for this purpose.</p>
<p>
<p style="text-align:right;">Prof. Pema Eden Samdup<br>Director, International Division</p>
</p></div>
