                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-8" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Newinitiatives"  ><p align="justify">The University is continuously working for expanding its reach and writes letters to Indian Embassies/High Commissions in various countries from time-to-time for their kind assistance for collaboration with institutes to recognize them as Overseas Study Centres.<ul>
<li>Under the e-VidyaBharati and e-AarogyaBharati(e-VBAB) Network Project of the Ministry of External Affairs, Government of India, the University is offering its 51 programmes online in 19 African countries. Later, Afghanistan was included in eVBAB Project.</li>
<li>The University offered a three-month online Basic Hindi Awareness programme for foreign nationals in collaboration with Indian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR), and Central Hindi Directorate (CHD) and registered students from 9 countries in the first batch and from 29 countries in the second batch. Recently, the University have successfully completed the third batch of three-month online Basic Hindi Awareness Course with registration from 42 countries</li>
<li>The University signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Open University of Kenya (OUK).</li>
<li>Further, the University also signed Memorandum of Collaboration (MoC) with the Baikal State University, Russia the Financial University, Moscow, Russia and the Hellenic Open University (HOU), Greece.</li>
<li>For promoting online programmes of the University internationally, the University come out with a scheme of “Overseas Facilitator” and Memorandum of Agreementshave been signed with 14 existing Overseas Study Centres in the first phase. Recently, Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) has been signed with ‘ICA, Education Pvt. Ltd. (ICAEPL), Nepal and Centre for Open and Distance Education, Kenya for Overseas Facilitator.</li>
<li>•	International Division renewed seven MoAs with the following Overseas Study Centre of the University:
o	Bridge Academy, Muscat, Sultanate of Oman 
o	Polyglot Institute, Muscat, Sultanate of Oman
o	Kuwait Educational Centre, Kuwait
o	Al Hikma Education Institution, Sharjah, UAE
o	Emirates Professional Training Institute, Sharjah, UAE
o	Central Asian Indian Institute Of Distance Education (CAIIDE), Kyrgyzstan
o	BakhtarUniversity,  Afghanistan</li>

<li>•he University organised 11th Overseas Coordinators Consortium Meet at the University Headquarters, New Delhi on 23rd and 24th September, 2024 for strengthening our relationship with Overseas Study Centres and to discuss various steps for enhancing IGNOU’s enrolment and outreach</li></ul></p></div>
